# WinClash STOCK MARKET bot: the paired-hedge commands (/pair, /pairs,
# /delpair, /run, /stoprun, /runs, /runlog) driving Evolution's "Stock Market
# Live" on winclash.com -- acc1 bets UP, acc2 bets DOWN on the same round, so
# money mostly moves between the two accounts. No signup commands (those live
# on .env.winclash), and no /testbaccarat.
#
# WHAT IS VERIFIED LIVE (2026-08-29), so nobody re-derives it:
#   * login()             -- real account, real session, confirmed through the
#                            site's own POST /api/getBalance.
#   * the table route     -- winclash has NO usable lobby tile for this; the
#                            engine navigates straight to the site's own
#                            /casinoRedirect launch URL (game id 1027). That
#                            lands on ezugi.evo-games.com with
#                            table_id=StockMarket00001 -- the same Evolution
#                            client every other site here uses.
#   * the whole read path -- verify_stockmarket.py PASSED end to end: table
#                            ready in ~37s, balance/portfolio/TOTAL BET all
#                            readable, chip rail 10/50/100/200/500/2500, and
#                            4 clean betting windows detected in 90 seconds.
#
# WHAT IS *NOT* VERIFIED, and it matters before any real run:
#   * NO BET HAS EVER BEEN PLACED ON THIS SITE. The only winclash account
#     available during development held 0.00, so placing, settling and the
#     hedge itself are untested here (everything above is a read).
#   * winclash's own tile handler REFUSES to open a table when both the real
#     and bonus balances are zero. The engine's direct route sidesteps that,
#     but a zero-balance account still cannot bet -- fund both accounts first.
#   * Which key of /api/getBalance carries the real figure. Both "wallet" and
#     "main_balance"/"totalBalance" read 0.00 on an empty account, which
#     cannot tell them apart. Check a funded account's reading against the
#     header before trusting a balance here.
#
# So: fund two accounts, run
#     .venv/bin/python verify_stockmarket.py <user> <pass> --url https://winclash.com/
# then a single "/run <pair> 10 1" (table minimum is 10 rupees) and read
# /runlog before scaling either the amount or the rounds.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-winclash-stockmarket-bot-token-from-botfather
# One id, or several comma-/space-separated ids for multiple master admins:
# MASTER_ADMIN_ID=111111111,222222222
MASTER_ADMIN_ID=your-telegram-user-id

# REQUIRED on winclash, unlike cricmatch/khelofun. Every page load here can be
# met by an AWS WAF interstitial; the soft "challenge" clears itself for free,
# but the hard "captcha" needs a solved token, and each seat's login pays one
# if it lands on that. Without a key a run fails with a clear message rather
# than hanging.
CAPSOLVER_API_KEY=your-capsolver-api-key

BOT_MODE=stockmarket
BOT_SITE_URL=https://winclash.com/
ADMINS_FILE=admins.winclash.stockmarket.json
SETTINGS_FILE=bot_settings.winclash.stockmarket.json
# Pair credentials + run history. MUST be distinct from every other
# instance's files -- each process reads them once at import and rewrites
# them whole on every save, so two bots sharing a path silently clobber
# each other. (pairs.* holds plaintext passwords; both patterns are
# gitignored.)
PAIRS_FILE=pairs.winclash.stockmarket.json
PAIR_RUNS_FILE=pair_runs.winclash.stockmarket.json

# How many /run hedge sessions may execute at once (each drives two Chromium
# browsers). Default 3.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=3
